===Alternative forms===
*[[elliptic]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ɪˈlɪp.tɪk.əl/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɪˈlɪp.tɪ.kəl/}}
* {{audio|en-us-elliptical.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# In a shape reminding of an [[ellipse]]; [[oval]].
# Of, or showing [[ellipsis]]; having a word or words omitted.
#:''If he is sometimes '''elliptical''' and obscure, it is because he has so much to tell us.'' -- [[w:Edmund Wilson|Edmund Wilson]]

====Usage notes====
In botanical usage, ''elliptic(al)'' refers only to the general shape of the [[leaf]], independently of its [[apex]] or [[margin]] (and sometimes the [[base]]), so that an "elliptic leaf"may very well be [[pointed]] at both ends.

